276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (Existing dynamic pricing algorithms optimize almost exclusively for profit in simulated environments, lacking an explicit mathematical penalty to reduce actual physical food waste. This omission means that spoilage is treated as an acceptable cost rather than a primary optimization target, resulting in algorithms that are commercially oriented but environmentally inadequate.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
